# Cursor Rules — DHF Repository
#
# Copy this file to the repo root as `.cursorrules` to enable Cursor IDE support.
# Content mirrors AI-harness/context.md — update both if the project context changes.

This repository is a Design History File (DHF) managed with CompliantFlow for medical device software compliance (IEC 62304, ISO 14971).

## Key rules

- All DHF mutations (create, update, lifecycle transitions) go through `python -m utils`, not direct file edits
- Compliance analysis uses the `compliantflow` CLI (read-only)
- Traceability edges run child → parent: SRS derives_from SYS, SYS derives_from CRS, etc.
- GitOps approval: UC, CRS, SYS, SRS, SWDD, SYSARCH, RISK, RCM, SOUP, TC are approved by landing on main
- Explicit lifecycle: CR, REL, DEF require `python -m utils item transition`
- Always create a CR item before making changes; include CR ID in branch name and PR title
- Run `PYTHONPATH=.:DHF python -m utils validate schema` before committing
- Run `compliantflow --dhf DHF validate traceability` before opening a PR

## Common commands

```bash
PYTHONPATH=.:DHF python -m utils item list --type SYS
PYTHONPATH=.:DHF python -m utils item create --type SRS --data '{"title": "...", "derives_from": ["SYS-001"]}'
PYTHONPATH=.:DHF python -m utils validate schema
compliantflow --dhf DHF validate traceability
compliantflow --dhf DHF status --governance-dir governance
```

See AI-harness/context.md for full reference.
